1
00:00:08,860 --> 00:00:10,360
I had an interview today, too.

2
00:00:10,360 --> 00:00:11,710
I had a great interview

3
00:00:11,710 --> 00:00:14,160
with Admissions at Columbia University.

4
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:15,090
Really?

5
00:00:15,090 --> 00:00:16,340
What did they say?

6
00:00:16,340 --> 00:00:17,780
Will you get into the school?

7
00:00:17,780 --> 00:00:19,810
Well, they didn't say anything for sure.

8
00:00:19,810 --> 00:00:23,610
But I figure that with my grades and with my personality,

9
00:00:23,610 --> 00:00:25,410
I'll have no problem.

10
00:00:25,410 --> 00:00:27,720
Columbia's a terrific school.

11
00:00:27,720 --> 00:00:29,050
What are you going to do?

12
00:00:29,050 --> 00:00:31,400
Do? I don't know.

13
00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:34,140
I also applied to NYU.

14
00:00:34,140 --> 00:00:36,450
You sound excited about Columbia.

15
00:00:36,450 --> 00:00:38,360
What's your problem, Mike?

16
00:00:38,360 --> 00:00:40,980
Indecision. Indecision.

17
00:00:40,980 --> 00:00:41,790
It's not easy,

18
00:00:41,790 --> 00:00:44,140
and this is an important decision we have to make.

19
00:00:44,140 --> 00:00:45,390
What about you?

20
00:00:45,390 --> 00:00:47,290
How was your interview with Michigan?

21
00:00:47,290 --> 00:00:48,900
The interview was fine.

22
00:00:48,900 --> 00:00:50,830
It's a great college.

23
00:00:50,830 --> 00:00:52,100
It is.

24
00:00:52,100 --> 00:00:54,040
My father would like me to go there.

25
00:00:54,040 --> 00:00:56,500
He and my Grandpa both went there.

26
00:00:56,500 --> 00:00:58,180
Great medical school, too.

27
00:00:58,180 --> 00:01:00,190
I know.

28
00:01:00,190 --> 00:01:02,340
You can follow in your father's footsteps.

29
00:01:02,340 --> 00:01:06,420
Ah! I'd like to follow in my own footsteps, Mike.

30
00:01:06,420 --> 00:01:08,190
What do you want to study?

31
00:01:08,190 --> 00:01:09,900
I've been thinking.

32
00:01:09,900 --> 00:01:12,220
I think I want to study journalism

33
00:01:12,220 --> 00:01:14,510
to be a reporter--a newspaperman.

34
00:01:14,510 --> 00:01:17,800
You do a pretty good job on the Riverdale High School paper.

35
00:01:17,800 --> 00:01:20,270
And I've been thinking about it a lot lately.

36
00:01:20,270 --> 00:01:22,330
Have you discussed it with your parents?

37
00:01:22,330 --> 00:01:25,350
No. But I have to.

38
00:01:25,350 --> 00:01:37,170
OK. Let's talk.

39
00:01:37,170 --> 00:01:41,860
Hi, Son. Is everything all right?

40
00:01:41,860 --> 00:01:44,820
Hi, Dad. Everything's fine.

41
00:01:44,820 --> 00:01:46,570
I was just waiting for you to get home

42
00:01:46,570 --> 00:01:47,640
so we could talk.

43
00:01:47,640 --> 00:01:50,450
Anything special you want to talk about?

44
00:01:50,450 --> 00:01:53,120
There is, Dad.

45
00:01:53,120 --> 00:01:55,220
I'm listening.

46
00:01:55,220 --> 00:01:59,420
Well, I know you and Mom have given up a lot

47
00:01:59,420 --> 00:02:02,660
to save money for my college tuition.

48
00:02:02,660 --> 00:02:04,240
We want you to go to college, Robbie.

49
00:02:04,240 --> 00:02:06,730
I know. I do.

50
00:02:06,730 --> 00:02:08,720
But?

51
00:02:08,720 --> 00:02:13,310
Well, I've thought a lot about which college,

52
00:02:13,310 --> 00:02:16,140
and one of them is Columbia.

53
00:02:16,140 --> 00:02:20,440
Columbia? Why Columbia?

54
00:02:20,440 --> 00:02:25,620
First, they have an excellent School of Journalism.

55
00:02:25,620 --> 00:02:27,840
They do.

56
00:02:27,840 --> 00:02:32,110
And your friends are planning to go to Columbia?

57
00:02:32,110 --> 00:02:34,370
That's only part of it.

58
00:02:34,370 --> 00:02:37,970
It's complicated.

59
00:02:37,970 --> 00:02:40,070
I'll try to explain.

60
00:02:40,070 --> 00:02:43,720
Mike and I had a hamburger this afternoon, and we talked.

61
00:02:43,720 --> 00:02:45,460
Yes?

62
00:02:45,460 --> 00:02:48,370
Well, we talked about a lot of things.

63
00:02:48,370 --> 00:02:49,710
He applied to Columbia,

64
00:02:49,710 --> 00:02:51,790
and his interview was very successful.

65
00:02:51,790 --> 00:02:53,160
He thinks he'll be accepted,

66
00:02:53,160 --> 00:02:56,690
and he really wants to go there.

67
00:02:56,690 --> 00:02:59,970
Dean Rafer called me today.

68
00:02:59,970 --> 00:03:03,990
He told me he was very impressed with you.

69
00:03:03,990 --> 00:03:05,320
He's a nice man.

70
00:03:05,320 --> 00:03:07,850
He was very kind.

71
00:03:07,850 --> 00:03:09,780
He told me

72
00:03:09,780 --> 00:03:13,550
you had some doubts about wanting to go to Michigan.

73
00:03:13,550 --> 00:03:15,880
Yes. I do.

74
00:03:15,880 --> 00:03:20,020
I'm just not sure about what I want to do.

75
00:03:20,020 --> 00:03:23,070
That's OK.

76
00:03:23,070 --> 00:03:25,310
You understand?

77
00:03:25,310 --> 00:03:28,040
Let me tell you something, Robbie.

78
00:03:28,040 --> 00:03:34,810
Something that might be surprising to you.

79
00:03:34,810 --> 00:03:39,410
What? Tell me.

80
00:03:39,410 --> 00:03:46,530
Well, Grandpa wanted me to study engineering, like him.

81
00:03:46,530 --> 00:03:49,420
Well, I wasn't clear about my future,

82
00:03:49,420 --> 00:03:55,840
but I knew engineering was not for me.

83
00:03:55,840 --> 00:03:59,180
What did you tell Grandpa?

84
00:03:59,180 --> 00:04:02,770
The truth.

85
00:04:02,770 --> 00:04:04,160
Then you're not upset

86
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:08,230
about my not wanting to go into medicine?

87
00:04:08,230 --> 00:04:10,650
I'm not upset at all.

88
00:04:10,650 --> 00:04:14,900
I'm just happy that we're able to talk about it.

89
00:04:14,900 --> 00:04:18,190
I am too, Dad.

90
00:04:18,190 --> 00:04:22,510
I suppose you want to apply to Columbia.

91
00:04:22,510 --> 00:04:28,750
Yes, but I also want to apply to several other colleges.

92
00:04:28,750 --> 00:04:30,500
I thought you wanted to go to Columbia.

93
00:04:30,500 --> 00:04:32,880
Well, I might want to go to Columbia.

94
00:04:32,880 --> 00:04:35,230
But I might not.

95
00:04:35,230 --> 00:04:39,530
I just want to be able to make my own decision.

96
00:04:39,530 --> 00:04:42,670
You're a real Stewart!

97
00:04:42,670 --> 00:04:47,060
And if I think about it long enough, you never know ...

98
00:04:47,060 --> 00:04:48,580
Never know what?

99
00:04:48,580 --> 00:04:51,780
If I make my own decision,

100
00:04:51,780 --> 00:04:56,980
I might choose Michigan.

101
00:04:56,980 --> 00:04:59,110
Robbie, you're something!

102
00:04:59,110 --> 00:05:02,660
You know, when I was your age,

103
00:05:02,660 --> 00:05:05,660
I said exactly the same thing to Grandpa.
